# Shell scripts must never get CRLF (a CRLF shebang line fails with "bad interpreter" on Linux),
# and sources, instruction text and JSON are LF everywhere so builds, embedded files and the
# instruction files agtk generates are identical on every checkout (Windows CI checks out with
# autocrlf, which turned base/AGENTS.md into CRLF and broke the GEMINI.md line-ending test).
*.sh   text eol=lf
*.go   text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
*.yml  text eol=lf
*.md   text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.toml text eol=lf
*.mjs  text eol=lf
*.golden text eol=lf

# Vendored skill packs keep the bytes they were pinned with: skills/baseline.json and the
# install pins hash them. A few of their files are CRLF in the index; do not rewrite those.
# This rule comes last so it wins over the patterns above.
packs/** -text
